    /// <summary>
    /// ## Void payment
    ///
    /// Voids a previously captured payment that has not yet been settled. Voids are typically used to cancel
    /// a transaction before funds are officially transferred. Unlike refunds, which occur after settlement,
    /// a void happens before the transaction is finalized on the customer's statement.
    ///
    /// Only payments that are in a `SUCCESSFUL` (captured) status and have not yet been settled can be voided.
    /// Once a payment is successfully voided, its status changes to `VOIDED`.
    /// </summary>
    /// <exception cref="global::WebFunction.Exceptions.BadRequestException">code "NOT_FOUND" - This error occurs when no payment with the provided ID exists in your merchant account. Double check that you're using the correct payment ID.</exception>
    /// <exception cref="global::WebFunction.Exceptions.BadRequestException">code "NOT_VOIDABLE" - Payment is not eligible for void. This can happen if the payment is not in a captured state, has already settled into a statement, the void window has passed, or the integration does not support voids.</exception>
    /// <exception cref="global::WebFunction.Exceptions.UnexpectedStatusCodeException">if the server responds with a non-200/400 status</exception>
    /// <exception cref="global::WebFunction.Exceptions.JsonParseException">if the response body isn't valid JSON</exception>
